  "id": "COMPOUND:711 - DISEASE:1998",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between trimipramine and Meningitis, Fungal, through a chain of biological interactions involving insulin receptor substrate 1. Trimipramine, a tricyclic antidepressant, is associated with side effects such as tongue discolouration and delusion, both of which are linked to olanzapine, an antipsychotic drug. Olanzapine affects insulin receptor substrate 1, which, when dysregulated, may contribute to the development of Meningitis, Fungal. The scores from the two paths indicate a moderate level of support for this relationship, with slight variations in confidence due to differences in the specific side effects and their associated pathways. The evidence is consistent across both paths, highlighting a mechanistic link between trimipramine and the condition, though further research is needed to confirm the causal relationship and its relevance in clinical settings.",
